.TH CFX 1 "August 1, 2026" "cfx" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
cfx \- small, auditable Codeforces workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.I problem
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B submit
.RB [ \-\-manual ]
.RB [ \-\-rebuild ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B test
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B stress
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B fail
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfx
manages an ordinary C++20 Codeforces solution archive.
The usual workflow is:
.PP
.nf
cfx 71A
cfx submit
.fi
.PP
The first command fetches the statement metadata and samples through the
browser connector, creates the problem directory, and opens
.IR solution.cpp .
The second tests and checked-compiles the exact bundled source, submits it
through the signed-in browser, and waits for the Codeforces verdict.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I problem
Fetch a problem, create
.IR codeforces/contest/index/ ,
open
.IR solution.cpp ,
and remember it as the current problem.
Official contest mirrors are tried when the primary statement is unavailable.
.TP
.BR test " [" problem "]"
Bundle and compile the solution, then run fetched samples followed by
handwritten cases.
Every input requires a matching expected-output file.
Report OK, WA, RE, TLE, MLE, or OLE with resource use.
.TP
.BR stress " [" problem "]"
Compile the solution, generator, and brute-force implementation.
Generate deterministic inputs and compare both outputs.
The default helper files are
.I stress/gen.cpp
and
.IR stress/brute.cpp .
The generator receives the seed as its final argument.
.TP
.BR fail " [" problem "]"
Promote the latest stress mismatch to
.I cases/stress-N.in
and
.IR cases/stress-N.out .
.TP
.BR submit " [" problem "]"
Run every saved test, checked-compile the exact bundled source, submit it
through Chrome, and report the verdict and official resource use.
Only
.B OK
on
.B TESTS
is Accepted.
.B PRETESTS
and known pending submissions exit 2; a final non-Accepted verdict exits 1.
When the connector is unavailable, copy the tested source to the clipboard and
open the submission page.
No password or session cookie is read or stored.
.TP
.BR help " [" command "]"
Display general help or help for one command.
.SH TEST OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-checked
Compile with strict warnings, AddressSanitizer, and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild
Ignore a cached binary.
.TP
.BI "\-\-time-limit " seconds
Override the fetched time limit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-memory-limit " MiB
Override the fetched memory limit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-output-limit " MiB
Override the output limit, which defaults to 64 MiB.
.SH STRESS OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-gen " file
Use another generator.
.TP
.BI "\-\-brute " file
Use another brute-force implementation.
.TP
.BR \-n " " count ", " \-\-count " " count
Run
.I count
generated tests; the default is 100.
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " number
Set the first seed; the default is 1.
.TP
.BI "\-\-gen-arg " argument
Pass an argument to the generator; may be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-checked
Checked-compile the solution and brute-force implementation.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild
Ignore cached binaries.
.TP
.BI "\-\-time-limit " seconds
Set the solution and brute-force timeout.
.TP
.BI "\-\-generator-time-limit " seconds
Set the generator timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print every seed result.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-manual
Copy the tested source to the clipboard and open the submission page instead
of using the connector.
.TP
.BI "\-\-root " directory
Use
.I directory
as the archive root.
.SH PROBLEM IDENTIFIERS
Explicit problems use only the canonical Codeforces form, for example
.BR 71A .
When run beneath
.IR codeforces/contest/index/ ,
commands infer the problem.
.B submit
may also use the most recently opened problem.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/solution.cpp
User solution.
.TP
.I .cfx/solution.cpp
Optional archive-owned starter template.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/cases/
Handwritten and promoted regression cases.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/stress/
Optional generator and brute-force source.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/problem.json
Fetched problem metadata and resource limits.
.TP
.I include/cp/
Extensionless, submission-safe competitive-programming headers.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cfx/workspaces/
Fetched samples, builds, run output, stress failures, current-problem state,
and prepared submissions.
When
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset, cfx uses
.IR $HOME/.local/state/cfx/workspaces/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CXX
C++ compiler command; the default is
.BR c++ .
.TP
.B CFX_STD
C++ language standard; the default is
.BR c++20 .
.TP
.B CFX_CXXFLAGS
Additional compiler flags.
.TP
.B CFX_ROOT
Explicit archive root.
.TP
.B CFX_STATE_ROOT
Explicit runtime-state root.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used for
.IR solution.cpp .
.TP
.B VISUAL
Editor fallback.
.TP
.B CFX_BROWSER
Browser-opening command override.
.TP
.B CFX_CLIPBOARD
Clipboard command override.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation succeeded; for
.BR submit ,
the verdict was
.B OK
on
.BR TESTS .
.TP
.B 1
Testing or stress checking failed, or submit received a final non-Accepted
verdict.
.TP
.B 2
Usage was invalid, an operation failed, or submission is pending or requires
manual completion.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch and solve a problem:
.PP
.nf
cfx 71A
cfx submit
.fi
.PP
Run sanitizer-backed tests:
.PP
.nf
cfx test --checked
.fi
.PP
Differential-test inputs and preserve a mismatch:
.PP
.nf
cfx stress -n 10000 --seed 1
cfx fail
cfx test
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR c++ (1),
.BR git (1)
